==Maltese==
{{mt-root|r-s-l}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|mt|ar|رَسُول}}. Called an “arabism” by Falzon, but this may mean merely that the word was already highly archaic in the mid-19th century. At any rate it was inherited, not introduced later by Muslim captives, because old sources show that the place {{m|mt||Għajn Rasul}} was always understood as “Spring of the Apostle [Paul]”.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|mt|/raˈsuːl/}}

===Noun===
{{mt-noun|g=m|p=rsul|p2=rsiel|p3=rsajjal|p4=irsla|p5=rosol}}

# {{tlb|mt|obsolete}} {{synonym of|mt|appostlu|t=apostle}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|mt|Għajn Rasul}}
* {{l|mt|rasuli}}